---
// Root `/` has no content of its own — locales are keyed `en`/`pt-br`
// (src/pages/[locale]/), not a root locale, so Starlight won't redirect here
// automatically.
//
// This site builds statically (no SSR adapter), so there's no request to
// read an Accept-Language header from at build time — the browser's
// language preference only exists once the page is running client-side.
// Redirect from inline script instead of Astro.redirect(), checking
// navigator.languages for a Portuguese tag and falling back to `en`.
//
// In production this page is never served: vercel.json redirects `/` on the
// server first (307, by the Accept-Language header's first language — the
// same rule as apps/app's preferredLocale()), which crawlers can follow and
// users don't see a blank flash for. This stays as the fallback for
// `astro dev`/`preview`, kept out of the index and the sitemap
// (astro.config.mjs).
---

<meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
<script is:inline>
  const prefersPortuguese = (navigator.languages ?? [navigator.language])
    .some((tag) => tag.toLowerCase().startsWith('pt'))
  window.location.replace(prefersPortuguese ? '/pt-br/' : '/en/')
</script>
<noscript>
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/en/" />
</noscript>
